{"name":"Tubbataha Teal","hex":"#0e8787","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"teal","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various small freshwater ducks of the genus Anas that are brightly coloured and have short necks.","A dark, somewhat bluish-green colour; a dark cyan."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Having a bluish-green colour."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/teal"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tubbataha Reef","blocks":[{"text":"The Tubbataha Natural Park, also known as the Tubbataha Reefs Natural Park, is a protected area of the Philippines located in the middle of the Sulu Sea. The marine and bird sanctuary consists of two huge atolls and the smaller Jessie Beazley Reef covering a total area of 97,030 hectares. It is located 150 kilometres (93 mi) southeast of Puerto Princesa, the capital of Palawan. The uninhabited islands and reefs are part of the island municipality of Cagayancillo, located roughly 130 kilometers (81 mi) to the northeast of the reef."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e1/Tubbataha_Shark.jpg/330px-Tubbataha_Shark.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tubbataha_Reef"},{"title":"Teal","blocks":[{"text":"Teal is a dark cyan color. Its name comes from that of a bird, the Eurasian teal which has a similarly colored stripe on its head. The word is often used colloquially to refer to shades of cyan in general."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1a/Smithsonian_-_NMAAHC_-_Teal_blue_dress_and_cropped_jacket_designed_by_Ann_Lowe-_NMAAHC_2014.73.2.1-.2.jpg/330px-Smithsonian_-_NMAAHC_-_Teal_blue_dress_and_cropped_jacket_designed_by_Ann_Lowe-_NMAAHC_2014.73.2.1-.2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teal"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Tubbataha_Ree